INSTALL — Batch Image Processing at Scale with CUDA NPP
=======================================================

Prerequisites
-------------
  * CUDA Toolkit 11.0 or newer (provides nvcc and the NPP libraries)
  * NPP libraries — bundled with the CUDA Toolkit, no separate install
  * An NVIDIA GPU with a compute capability supported by your toolkit
  * Linux (x86_64). Other platforms with CUDA may work but are untested.
  * Python 3 with Pillow — only needed to generate synthetic test images
        pip install Pillow

Verify your toolchain
---------------------
  nvcc --version        # should report CUDA 11.0+
  nvidia-smi            # should list your GPU

Build
-----
  make                  # produces bin/npp_processor

Run
---
  bash run.sh           # builds if needed, generates test data, runs pipeline

  Or run the binary directly:
  ./bin/npp_processor -i data/input/ -o data/output/ -p full -v

Clean
-----
  make clean            # removes object files and the binary

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * "cannot find -lnppif" etc.: ensure the CUDA lib directory is on your
    linker path, e.g.
        export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/cuda/lib64:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH
    and that CUDA's bin directory is on PATH for nvcc.
  * "no CUDA-capable device": confirm the driver is installed (nvidia-smi).
